      "observed": "REG1.1 and REG1.2 connect to +3.3V, while the separate +3V3 net has no regulator output connected to it. The FCC and NAVC MCU VDD pins and analog supply pins are shown as unconnected rather than tied to either rail.",
      "expected": "The specification says the LD39200 produces the 3.3 V rail for the MCUs and sensors. That rail must be connected to the MCU supply pins; the regulator output and intended 3V3 distribution must be electrically continuous.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\")) (node (ref \"REG1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"ADJ/SENSE\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC2-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VDD-Pad19)\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "A 3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) ... produces 3V3 for “MCUs and Sensors”"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator output is not connected to the named +3V3 distribution, and the MCU supply pins are unconnected in the netlist. As represented, the MCUs cannot be powered correctly, so the board will not perform its intended flight-control functions.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC2", "UART3_FCC2", "C23"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.48", "FCC2.73", "UART3_FCC2.3", "UART3_FCC2.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0082", "NET0116", "unconnected-(C23-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "Both FCC2 VCAP pins are routed to pins on the UART3_FCC2 connector: FCC2.48 to connector pin 3 and FCC2.73 to pin 4. C23 is listed as unconnected.",
      "expected": "VCAP is an MCU internal-regulator supply pin and should have its required local capacitor connection, not be exposed on UART connector signal pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"NET0082\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"71\") (name \"NET0116\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"166\") (name \"unconnected-(C23-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C23\") (pin \"1\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector pins carry the MCU's VCAP nets rather than usable UART signals, and the required VCAP decoupling is not evident. This can prevent correct MCU operation and make the UART connection unusable.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the 3.3 V regulator output and the +3V3 distribution are separate nets, and the MCU supply pins are shown unconnected. The FCC VCAP pins are also routed to UART connector pins instead of being properly decoupled."
}

